_struct_biol.id                    1 
_struct_biol.details               
;THE ENZYME IS A HEXADECAMER L8S8 OF EIGHT L (LARGE) SUBUNIT
AND 8 S (SMALL) SUBUNITS.  THE L SUBUNIT HAS BEEN ASSIGNED
CHAIN IDENTIFIERS A, B, C, D, E, F, G, AND H.  THE S
SUBUNIT HAS BEEN ASSIGNED CHAIN IDENTIFIERS I, J, K, L, M,
N, O, AND P.  IN THE CATALYTICALLY COMPETENT MOLECULE,
DIMERS OF THE LARGE SUBUNITS FORM FUNCTIONAL UNITS.  IN
REFERENCE 1 THESE DIMERS ARE DESIGNATED *AB*, *CD*, *EF*,
AND *GH*.

THIS ENTRY PRESENTS THE CRYSTALLOGRAPHIC ASYMMETRIC UNIT
WHICH CONTAINS HALF THE MOLECULE: FOUR L AND FOUR S
SUBUNITS RELATED BY A FOUR-FOLD AXIS THROUGH THE MOLECULAR
CENTER AT X=0, Y=1/4, Z=1/4.  THE FOUR L CHAINS PRESENT
ARE A, C, E, G AND THE FOUR S CHAINS PRESENT ARE
I, J, K, L.  ALSO INCLUDED ARE FOUR MAGNESIUM IONS, FOUR
INHIBITOR MOLECULES (CAP) AND 1520 WATERS.
;
_struct_biol.pdbx_parent_biol_id   ? 
